      "tag": "Stop 1",
      "h2": "Why save?",
      "body_html": "<p class=\"big\"><span class=\"hl p\">Saving</span> means you can buy bigger things later — and you're ready when things go wrong.</p><p>Even £1 a week becomes £52 in a year. 💷</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Stop 2",
      "h2": "Interest helps",
      "body_html": "<p>Banks pay <span class=\"hl p\">interest</span> on savings.</p><p>£200 at 5% = <b>£10</b> a year.</p><p><span class=\"hl y\">Compound interest</span> means next year you earn interest on £210 — so it grows faster every year. 📈</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Stop 3",
      "h2": "Save like a pro",
      "body_html": "<p>Tips that work:</p><ul><li>Set a <b>goal</b> — a bike, a console.</li><li>Save first, spend second.</li><li>Keep an <b>emergency fund</b> for surprises.</li><li>Don't dip in unless it's the goal.</li></ul></p>"
    }
